## 🔧 Raspberry Pi Setup Instructions

To run the MP3 loop player on boot with GPIO button control, install the following packages:

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y \
    python3 \
    python3-rpi.gpio \
    mpg123 \
    alsa-utils \
    thonny
```

## 📂 Audio File Locations

Make sure these MP3 files exist in the following directory:

```
/home/COCCedu2024/Downloads/mariosoundtrack.mp3
/home/COCCedu2024/Downloads/carsoundtrack.mp3
/home/COCCedu2024/Downloads/katyperrysoundtrack.mp3
```

## 🖥️ Autostart the Script on Boot (Desktop Mode Only)

Create an autostart entry:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/autostart
nano ~/.config/autostart/soundplayer.desktop
```

Paste the following:

```
[Desktop Entry]
Type=Application
Name=Sound Player
Exec=python3 /home/COCCedu2024/sound_cycle_button.py
StartupNotify=false
```

Save with `Ctrl+X`, then `Y`, then `Enter`.

Make sure the script is executable:

```bash
chmod +x /home/COCCedu2024/sound_cycle_button.py
```

Reboot to test:

```bash
sudo reboot
``

The "plank" soundtrack will start automatically and cycle to the next track with each press of the button connected to GPIO 17 (pin 11) and GND (pin 14).

